/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-710","Arturia's manual and Ableton/Live name the same three notes C1, C2 and C3.",["Octave key range reference","When the OLED shows -1"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-793","Every octave",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-812","The center key is the C in the middle of the keyboard, the 13th key from the left.",["Octave key range reference","Every octave"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-1462","Arturia and Ableton octave numbers",["Octave key range reference"]],["Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03%20Bottom/01%20Octave/Ref/Key%20Range/","source-block-1503","Arturia's manual and Ableton Live name MIDI note 60 C3, so each of their octave numbers is one below scientific pitch notation. The MicroFreak 5.0 manual gives the full MIDI range, notes 0 to 127, as C−2 to G8 in Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/01 as Soundgen.",["Octave key range reference","Arturia and Ableton octave numbers"]]],"format_version":5}